---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import orbitLogo from '../../assets/Ez Kyosk Orbit Logo.png';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DemoCTA from '../components/DemoCTA.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/sitePath';
---
<Layout title="About EZ Kyosk | Self-Ordering Software Philippines" description="Learn how EZ Kyosk approaches self-ordering, checkout, payments, inventory, and configurable customer experiences for Philippine businesses.">
  <section class="page-hero text-hero section-shell"><div class="page-hero-copy" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">About EZ Kyosk · Made for the ordering moment</span><h1>Simple for customers.<br /><span>Adaptable for business.</span></h1><p>EZ Kyosk brings the customer-facing order and the operational flow closer together—without making the experience feel complicated.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={sitePath('/contact/')}>Meet the product <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={sitePath('/features/')}>Explore features</a></div></div><div class="about-logo-panel" data-reveal><Image src={orbitLogo} alt="Official EZ Kyosk logo with turquoise kiosk symbol" width={900} format="webp" quality={90} /><p>Your Menu. Their Order. One Simple Screen.</p></div></section>
  <section class="about-story section-shell" data-reveal><div><span class="eyebrow">What EZ Kyosk does</span><h2>A focused experience with connected capability.</h2></div><div><p>EZ Kyosk is self-ordering and checkout kiosk software for businesses that want a clearer path from customer choice to operational action.</p><p>The core scope covers self-ordering, POS checkout, AltPayNet payment processing, real-time inventory, and order queueing or tracking. Reports, analytics, customer tools, loyalty, promotions, and other features can be configured to client requirements.</p><p>Hospitality and food are the initial focus, with room to support retail, wellness, beauty, service, B2B, and other suitable markets.</p></div></section>
  <section class="values-section section-shell" aria-labelledby="values-title" data-reveal><div class="section-heading inverse"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">How we think</span><h2 id="values-title">Four principles behind the experience.</h2></div><p>Good kiosk software should be easy to understand, accurate about what it offers, and flexible enough to fit the people using it.</p></div><div class="value-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Simplicity</h3><p>Keep the next action clear and reduce unnecessary friction in the customer journey.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Hospitality</h3><p>Use technology to support service—not to erase the human experience around it.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Adaptability</h3><p>Configure the system around the operation and its verified requirements.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Clarity</h3><p>Describe capabilities, compatibility, pricing, and implementation scope without unsupported promises.</p></article></div></section>
  <DemoCTA />
</Layout>
